{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Startup and shutdown: the ordered component table",
  "description": "How cmd/janus starts its components in order, stops them in reverse, and rolls back a failed start.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/main.go",
      "line": 16,
      "title": "The server starts",
      "description": "`func main` loads the settings and runs the application until it is told to stop."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/services.go",
      "line": 123,
      "title": "The ordered table",
      "description": "`func (a *application) groups` lists the groups in order: foundation, identity, projects and builds, runtime, web. Adding a component is one entry here."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/lifecycle.go",
      "line": 19,
      "title": "A component",
      "description": "`type component struct` has a name, a start and a stop. Either can be missing."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/lifecycle.go",
      "line": 47,
      "title": "Starting in order",
      "description": "`func (l *lifecycle) Start` runs the groups in order, and rolls back what already started if one fails."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/services.go",
      "line": 81,
      "title": "The application's start",
      "description": "`func (a *application) Start` opens the telemetry and the store, then starts the groups through the lifecycle."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/lifecycle.go",
      "line": 83,
      "title": "Stopping in reverse",
      "description": "`func (l *lifecycle) Stop` stops the components in reverse order, so the HTTP server stops taking requests before the stores and jobs drain."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/services.go",
      "line": 109,
      "title": "The application's stop",
      "description": "`func (a *application) Stop` records the shutdown in a span and calls the lifecycle's stop."
    }
  ]
}
